# Every text file is LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a clone on a machine where core.autocrlf is true — which is the
# default the Git for Windows installer sets — checks every file out with CRLF
# endings. Nothing in the repository has changed and the format check fails on
# all of it, along with any test that compares a file against text it built.
#
# The fix has to live here rather than in anybody's git config, because the
# person it breaks for is the person who has just cloned it and has not read
# anything yet.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The lockfile and the generated documents are text too, and are checked byte
# for byte against what the tools write, so they are the ones this matters most
# for.
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
